# Installing this package leaves three files on disk and changes nothing about
# the phone until two commands are run, and until 2026-09-18 nothing said so --
# `pacman -Qi moarchy-waydroid` looked like a working Waydroid and produced an
# Android nav bar eating 54 logical pixels inside every app window.
#
# Not an automated hook: both steps need a live graphical session (the setup
# script reads the output rect and the container's inset frames, and reloads
# sway), and a pacman transaction has neither.

post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

moarchy-waydroid is installed. Two steps, in this order:

  1. waydroid init                                  # ~1 GB unless the images
                                                    # are preinstalled
  2. waydroid session start                         # in the phone's session
     /usr/lib/moarchy/bin/moarchy-waydroid-setup    # pins the display and
                                                    # writes the sway rule
     waydroid session stop                          # the size is latched at
                                                    # calibration, so this is
                                                    # not optional

Re-run moarchy-waydroid-setup if the scale, the panel, the bar or the strip
ever changes: every number it writes is computed from the device.

Android apps then appear in the appDrawer on their own. Launch them from there --
the appDrawer routes them through moarchy-android-launch, and `waydroid app
launch` by hand gives up the status bar inset (docs/android.md AC 11).

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  # The 0.4.x watcher is gone and its unit with it. Leaving an enabled unit
  # behind would fail on every session start, and it would keep forcing
  # immersive.full=* until it did.
  if systemctl --user --global is-enabled moarchy-waydroid-immersive.service >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    cat <<'MSG'

moarchy-waydroid-immersive is gone (docs/android.md AC 6, AC 11). If you
enabled it by hand, disable it -- it forces the Android bars hidden, which is
what removes the insets the app needs:

  systemctl --user disable --now moarchy-waydroid-immersive.service

MSG
  fi
}
